      "description": {
        "fun": "Snorlax wakes up only to eat, about 400 kg of food a day, then goes straight back to sleep, often right across a road or bridge. Its stomach can handle anything, even mouldy food. It's gentle enough to let children bounce on its belly, but when one wanders into a village and empties the rice store, it's a disaster. Its Japanese name, Kabigon, nods to a Game Freak staff member nicknamed 'Kirby' for his appetite.",
        "guide": "A huge, dark blue-green Normal Pokémon that spends most of its time asleep and wakes only to eat. It evolves from Munchlax and is the heaviest Normal-type Pokémon. In several games it blocks the player's path until woken with a Poké Flute, and it can Gigantamax.",
